<div class="row justify-content-center"><div class="col-lg-8"><h1 class="fw-bold mb-2" style="font-size:clamp(2rem,5vw,3rem)">How HEALTHKEY uses your information</h1><p class="text-muted">Plain-language summary for this prototype. It is not legal advice.</p>
<div class="prose">
<h4 class="fw-bold mt-4">What we store</h4><p>Your account details, and the health information you choose to enter: blood type, allergies, conditions, medication, doctor, emergency contact and optional notes. We ask for your consent when you register because health information is sensitive personal data under Malaysia's Personal Data Protection Act 2010.</p>
<h4 class="fw-bold mt-4">Who can see it</h4><p>Anyone who scans your QR sees your emergency page, so only enter what you are comfortable showing a stranger in an emergency. Private notes are hidden unless you switch sharing on. Staff can see profile data only to run the service.</p>
<h4 class="fw-bold mt-4">The NFC tag</h4><p>If you write the NFC text to a tag, anyone who taps that tag can read it, and it cannot be switched off remotely. We only generate the essentials, and you choose which optional lines to include.</p>
<h4 class="fw-bold mt-4">The AI assistant</h4><p>Questions you type are sent to Google's Gemini service to produce answers. Your health profile is sent only if you tick “Use my health profile”. On the free tier, Google may use inputs to improve its products.</p>
<h4 class="fw-bold mt-4">Your controls</h4><p>Edit your profile at any time, pause or replace your QR from My QR, and delete your account from Account settings. Deleting removes your profile, orders, appointments, chats and QR.</p>
